      "notes": "Policy-compliant four-B70 single-session DeepSeek V4 Flash K160 MTP1 record. The checkpoint-attached one-layer MTP drafts one token and the unchanged target verifies every accepted token. Initial MTP reached 50.74/50.10 tok/s but failed a sustained exact replay by leaking prompt text after 437, so it was rejected. The repair executes the two verifier compressor rows as two exact M=1 FP32 projections; 20/20 ordered exact captures then pass, including ten after two long cold suites. The qualified strict suites reach 50.016860 and 49.420459 tok/s median versus the corrected 40.170350 nonspeculative base. All 24 realistic rows and 120 exact rows report cached_tokens=0. Measured cumulative MTP acceptance is 1,553/2,006 (77.4%). Four worker maps load the selected hashed oneCCL 2021.17.2 runtime; large prefill all-reduces retain the 128 KiB safe route. No prefix cache, history, or response reuse. K160 remains an experimental hash-pruned performance artifact."
